{"title":"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Postman Pete has a pedometer to count his steps. The pedometer records up to 99999 steps, then flips over to 00000 on the next step. Pete plans to determine his mileage for a year. On January 1 Pete sets the pedometer to 00000. During the year, the pedometer flips from 99999 to 00000 forty-four \ntimes. On December 31 the pedometer reads 50000. Pete takes 1800 steps per mile. Which of the following is closest to the number of miles Pete walked during the year?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/1268b5ea4783fdd9588b0668ca7f433dd7db26cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 2500\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 3000\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 3500\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 4000\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 4500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"478\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every time the pedometer flips from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a2f56dd0e57cb4603f97bc19530bf036969f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99999$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a15d522e9299ff10f38a48009273ffad9264e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$00000$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> Pete has walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1c9cc35374b57f3e393a898263c4cda825e912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> steps.\n</p><p>So, if the pedometer flipped <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times\n</p><p>Pete walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd8c0bf9183edf1f8938aef4cb504a9020b031f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44*100000+50000=4450000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"244\" height=\"14\" /> steps.\n</p><p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa858c71f0659dbdb750259e38da3ead33c96b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1800$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> steps per mile gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965b8b575bcc1ba256b57356d1bdfb58f1c4345a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2472.\\overline{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>This is closest to answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B\">2008 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B 